# Root build-context ignore. The release pipeline's server image builds
# from the STAGED context (tmp/docker-context/<arch>/fabro, staged by
# cargo dev docker-build), so this file governs the OTHER root-context
# builds — chiefly the engine's environment builds (ADR-0042: the
# toolchain image cooks over the run's checkout; the engine feeds the
# inline dockerfile text, so per-Dockerfile ignore overrides never
# apply — the root file is the only lever). It therefore allows the
# repo tree and excludes only the heavyweight, machine-local
# directories no cook reads. History: this file was once `*`-exclusive
# with staged allows (the release-pipeline shape); that starved every
# root-context build — the first live cooks all died at COPY "not
# found" (2026-11-10, denkhaus/work#1252). The local image build's
# staged context stays allowed (`!tmp/docker-context/**`) — the first
# relaxation dropped it and broke `just up` the same day.
.git
target
tmp/*
!tmp/docker-context/**
node_modules
dist
.fabro/cook
.fabro/judgments
# Live credentials never ride a build context (rust-security review,
# sprint 85): dev machines carry real keys in the untracked .env — not
# reachable today (the cook COPYs explicit paths and the engine packs a
# fresh clone), but one `COPY . .` must not ship them. The tracked
# .env.example stays context-visible.
.env
